EVALUATION.md §1 (stage E, CODEGEN.md §5.6; gen/go dependentLiteralFormat): baked gen/go writes a dependent type but no literal of one, so a selected value holding a dependent value is DependentType at the value; a value whose dependent field is none writes none.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// A payload.
type P(k: K) = match k { one => Int, two => String }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its kind.
  k: K
  /// Its payload.
  p: P(k)?
}

/// Holds a payload.
let full: Thing = { k: one, p: 1 }

/// Holds none.
let empty: Thing = { k: two }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- a.full.json --
{"k": "one", "p": 1}
-- a.empty.json --
{"k": "two"}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:18:5
  emit go in baked mode cannot generate a dependent type

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
